---
description: API, auth, routing, and form conventions
globs: src/**/*.{ts,tsx}
alwaysApply: false
---

# API

Never call Axios from UI. Flow: Component → feature hook → service → `apiClient.ts` → ASP.NET API.

Handle loading, empty, validation, network, server, and 401 errors with user-friendly messages. No `alert()`. No hard-coded API URLs; use `VITE_API_BASE_URL`.

# Auth

Use the existing Auth Context. Do not create a second auth system.

- Unauthenticated + protected page → Login
- Authenticated but wrong role → Unauthorized
- Enforce this in `ProtectedRoute`, not only by hiding UI

Add new routes in `routes/AppRoutes.tsx`. Protect and authorize there.

# Forms

Use React Hook Form + Zod. Include required validation, submit loading, and error/success feedback.

Destructive actions need Cancel / Delete confirmation.

# TypeScript

No `any`. Share types; do not duplicate the same interface in multiple files.
